# <type>(<scope>): Sentence case summary, under 72 characters
#
# Then a blank line, then the body: why this change exists.
#
# The diff already says what changed. What it cannot say is the problem being solved,
# the constraint that ruled out the obvious approach, or the failure mode that
# odd-looking line prevents. Write that, in prose.
#
# type: feat fix refactor docs chore test style ci perf build revert
# scope (optional): a crate or a command: core git store cli walk stats ...
#
# feat -> minor bump, fix perf revert -> patch, feat! or a BREAKING CHANGE: footer -> major
# (minor while the version is below 1.0). Everything else bumps nothing.
# Release Please owns every version; never edit one.
#
# Enable this template with:  git config commit.template .gitmessage
